<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sukhra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 493</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Zarmihr</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sukhra, also called Zarmihr, was a Sasanian nobleman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-karen">House of Karen</a> who dominated the Iranian court in the 480s. After King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peroz-i">Peroz I</a> was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hephthalites">Hephthalites</a> in 484, he restored order, raised Peroz's brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balash">Balash</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kavad-i">Kavad I</a> to the throne and governed as chief minister. Kavad, resenting his power, had him put to death around 493 with the help of Shapur of the House of Mihran.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sukhra.jpg" alt="Sukhra" width="319" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sufaray_(The_Shahnama_of_Shah_Tahmasp).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
